# Canonical author identity.
#
# Every identity below is the same person. They accumulated from different
# machines and git configs over the life of the repo.
#
# `leak-proof-test <test@example.invalid>` is not a contributor at all: it was
# an ad-hoc repo-local git identity set while developing the leak-scan hook on
# 2026-07-27, which then silently authored the next ten commits before anyone
# noticed. The local override has been removed, so new commits are attributed
# correctly. The ten published commits cannot be re-authored without rewriting
# public history and force-pushing, so they are reconciled here instead.
#
# `git shortlog`, `git blame`, `git log --use-mailmap` and GitHub's contributor
# graph all honour this file.

